Notebook[{
Cell["Hypermatrix", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"a0e84003-3405-a544-86a8-0b3fa989296c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8bc254ca-e6b6-b04d-a483-a2d2183ddf92"],
 " ",
 "represents the given arrays as a hypermatrix, holding them in canonical \
order."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"fe0405e6-3dbb-fc45-8a98-fa15468e6d03"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "85d4cfc5-5cfd-2e48-ad6c-ae1f78d6f74c"],
 " ",
 "is equivalent."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"a1893f0c-5c2c-ed40-b115-243606e9e9b8"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"966f2217-8c03-cb4d-b4df-4123e3968abb"],

Cell["\<\
The arrays are ordered by array order, lowest first; then by dimensions, \
shorter first, compared term by term; then by symmetry, taking \"Symmetric\" \
before \"Cyclic\" before \"Rigid\".\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"003950ed-f668-3543-ba92-f3ae27f74587"],

Cell["\<\
Two arrays alike in all three are put in the Wolfram Language's own canonical \
order, so that a hypermatrix is a function of the set of arrays it was given \
and of nothing else. Giving the same arrays in a different order produces the \
identical expression.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2d12b559-6cc1-3a40-afa5-ebeff8399e71"],

Cell["\<\
An irregular array is necessarily \"Rigid\", since only a regular array can \
carry a symmetry, so the symmetry criterion separates the regular arrays \
among themselves.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"dc6ba5c9-54f9-de4c-a8f9-e4e1fe8895f1"],

Cell["\<\
Numerical and symbolic arrays may be mixed freely. Raw entries given in place \
of an array are promoted to a NumericalArray.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b315b875-74e3-7a4f-8d7a-dc796d7aa49c"],

Cell["\<\
Length gives the number of arrays, and Normal the entries of each of them in \
order.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1ba4a0b0-9677-0046-bd54-7b7bf44a16ba"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"e0e3a582-5fc2-3948-9d5a-f4b44a1f72d2"],

Cell["The arrays are sorted whatever order they are given in:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"803fe682-806b-e84a-b0a2-e0c7e1bd0bc7"],

Cell["\<\
hm = Hypermatrix[{
   NumericalArray[Array[1 &, {2, 2, 2}], Automatic, \"Symmetric\"],
   NumericalArray[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}],
   NumericalArray[{1, 2}],
   NumericalArray[{1, 2, 3}],
   NumericalArray[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, Automatic, \"Symmetric\"],
   NumericalArray[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, Automatic, \"Cyclic\"]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3a8e1817-8ccf-2846-bd1b-ed7f09d3a16c"],

